I want to build a CLI which is a python package to be hosted on PyPI.
The CLI should help user create a github repo from command line. It should receive repo name(mandatory), repo description(optional) and github token(optional) as arguments.
If no repo description is provided, it should keep that field empty.
If no github token is provided, it should fall back to .env file in current folder.(You can assume the ADMIN_TOKEN required for github API is present in .env file in current project folder)
Also add documentation .
